<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26611" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lĭlybaeum</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ŏn</span></b>  (<i><span class="en">Ov. M. 13,
		726</span></i>), i, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λιλύβαιον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a promontory on the southern coast of Sicily, with a
				town of the same name</i>, now <i>Capo
				Bœo</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 8,
				14, § 87</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. in
				Caecil. 12, 39</span></i>; <i><span class="en">17, 56</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 25,
			31</span></i>; <i><span class="en">27, 5</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Ov.
				M. 5, 351 al.</span></i>—Called also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lĭlybē</span></b> ,
				ēs, f., acc. to the Gr.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λιλύβη</span>,
				<i><span class="en">Prisc. Perieg.
			482</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lĭlybaetānus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>adj., Lilybæan, of
				Lilybæum</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyso Lilybaetanus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 13, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulier,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Div. in Caecil. 17</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lĭlybaeus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., Lilybæan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					4, 583</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lĭlybēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj.,
			Lilybæan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vada,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 706</span></i>
			.</div>
